---
import CodeBlock from '../../../components/CodeBlock.astro'
import DocsLayout from '../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro'

const nativeExample = `import { launchBrowser, createBroadcast } from 'suitecut'

const url = process.env.SUITECUT_STREAM_URL
if (!url) throw new Error('Set SUITECUT_STREAM_URL')
const source = await launchBrowser({ width: 1920, height: 1080, framesPerSecond: 60 })
let broadcast
try {
  await source.navigate('https://example.com')
  broadcast = await createBroadcast({ source, stream: { url, audio: true } })
  await broadcast.ready()
  await Promise.race([
    source.failure, broadcast.failure,
    new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 30_000)),
  ])
} finally {
  await broadcast?.stop()
  await source.close()
}`

const example = `import { record } from 'suitecut/playwright'

const url = process.env.SUITECUT_STREAM_URL
if (!url) throw new Error('Set SUITECUT_STREAM_URL')

const controller = new AbortController()
process.once('SIGINT', () => controller.abort())

await record('live website tour', async ({ page, suitecut }) => {
  await page.goto('https://example.com')
  await suitecut.hold(30_000)
}, {
  signal: controller.signal,
  capture: {
    viewport: { width: 1280, height: 720 },
    deviceScaleFactor: 2,
    framesPerSecond: 30,
    stream: {
      url,
      size: { width: 1280, height: 720 },
      bitrateKbps: 4500,
      audio: true,
      onDiagnostic: (event) => console.log(event.event, event.bottleneck),
      reconnect: { initialDelayMs: 1000, maxDelayMs: 30_000, maxAttempts: 10 },
    },
  },
})`
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Live streaming"
  description="Publish a browser page over RTMP or RTMPS, recover from disconnects, and control live visual effects."
  section="streaming"
>
  <h1>Live streaming</h1>
  <p>
    Publish an embedded CEF browser to RTMP or RTMPS with SuiteCut 2.0. Native broadcasts use
    <code>launchBrowser</code> and <code>createBroadcast</code> from the root package. Existing Playwright
    streams use <code>capture.stream</code> through <code>suitecut/playwright</code>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="publish-a-page">Publish a page</h2>
  <p>
    Build the pinned CEF browser and set <code>SUITECUT_NATIVE_EXECUTABLE</code> as described in
    <a href="../docs#install">Getting started</a>. Native support is verified on macOS Apple
    Silicon. Set <code>SUITECUT_STREAM_URL</code> to your ingest URL, including its stream key.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock code={nativeExample} lang="typescript" />
  <p>
    The broadcast owns the publisher; the caller owns the source. Always stop and close both.
    Observe both failure promises. <code>stream.audio: true</code> sends CEF page audio directly. Native
    streaming does not mix synthesized narration or apply the final renderer's zoom transforms.
  </p>
  <h3>Existing Playwright streams</h3>
  <p>
    Run <code>npx playwright install chromium</code>, <code>npx suitecut install</code>, and
    <code>npx suitecut doctor</code> to prepare the browser and media tools. Set <code
      >SUITECUT_STREAM_URL</code
    > to the complete publish URL from your streaming service, including its stream key.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock code={example} lang="typescript" />
  <p>
    Publishing starts before the callback and stops when it returns or the session is aborted. The
    capture options also work in Playwright Test through <code>suitecutCapture</code>, except tab
    audio. Use one publisher per stream key. Disable parallel tests and retries that target the same
    key. RTMP is an ingest protocol; browser playback needs a media server or streaming service.
  </p>

  <h2 id="stream-options">Stream options</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>url</code>: required RTMP or RTMPS publish URL.</li>
    <li><code>bitrateKbps</code>: 100 through 50,000, default 4500.</li>
    <li>
      <code>audio</code>: boolean, default <code>false</code>. Set <code>true</code> for Chromium tab
      audio.
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>adaptiveBitrate</code>: enabled by default. Set <code>false</code> for fixed bitrate.
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>onDiagnostic</code>: receives a <code>LiveStreamDiagnostic</code> for congestion and bitrate
      changes.
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>size</code>: fixed output width and height, defaulting to the capture size. Both must be
      even, with a maximum of 7680 by 4320. Pages are letterboxed to fit.
    </li>
    <li><code>capture.framesPerSecond</code>: 30 or 60, default 30.</li>
    <li><code>capture.quality</code>: JPEG quality 1 through 100, default 90 for streaming.</li>
    <li>
      <code>capture.deviceScaleFactor</code>: 1 through 4. The browser preserves its CSS viewport
      and renders at the requested device-pixel density before the stream encoder downsamples with
      Lanczos.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The output is H.264 video with stereo AAC at 48 kHz. Keep stream keys in environment variables.
    SuiteCut omits publish URLs and encoder stderr from manifests and diagnostic events.
    Fixed-bitrate publishing passes the URL to FFmpeg's local process arguments.
  </p>

  <h2 id="tab-audio">Capture tab audio</h2>
  <p>
    <code>audio: true</code> captures the selected page through an isolated Chromium profile and bundled
    extension. Use the standalone <code>record()</code> API with current Playwright Chromium. Headed and
    headless modes work. Firefox, WebKit, custom executables, blocked service workers, and the Playwright
    Test fixture reject tab audio. Separate popup windows are unsupported; popups opened as tabs work.
  </p>
  <p>
    Audio follows page selection and navigation. Switching pages discards queued sound from the old
    page. Pausing capture sends silence, and resuming uses current audio. The isolated browser
    enables autoplay. Microphone input and synthesized narration are not mixed into the stream.
  </p>

  <h2 id="adaptive-bitrate">Adaptive bitrate and diagnostics</h2>
  <p>
    SuiteCut measures socket backpressure and lowers video bitrate during sustained network
    congestion. It prepares a replacement H.264 encoder and switches at a keyframe while keeping the
    RTMP publisher and AAC encoder alive. Audio timestamps continue across the handoff. Failed
    replacements leave the previous encoder running. Bitrate recovers gradually after five healthy
    minutes, up to the configured maximum.
  </p>
  <p>
    Temporary congestion discards stale capture data with bounded audio and video buffers. Twenty
    seconds without output progress triggers reconnection. Set
    <code>adaptiveBitrate: false</code> to use the fixed-bitrate FFmpeg path.
    <code>reconnect: false</code> disables reconnection, but does not disable bitrate handoffs.
  </p>
  <p>
    <code>onDiagnostic</code> reports capture lag, processing and write durations, output progress, socket
    backlog, and the current bottleneck. <code>bitrate-changing</code> announces preparation,
    <code>bitrate-adjusted</code> confirms the handoff, and <code>bitrate-change-failed</code> reports
    a failed replacement. Keep handlers short. Exceptions in the handler do not stop the stream.
  </p>

  <h2 id="reconnect-and-stop">Reconnect and stop</h2>
  <p>
    Disconnected or stalled encoders retry with exponential backoff. The default delay starts at one
    second and reaches a maximum of 30 seconds. Set <code>reconnect.initialDelayMs</code> and
    <code>reconnect.maxDelayMs</code> to change those delays. Set <code>reconnect.maxAttempts</code>
    to limit consecutive retries; its default of zero retries indefinitely. A connection lasting at least
    30 seconds resets the budget. Set <code>reconnect: false</code> to disable retries.
  </p>
  <p>
    The callback waits for the first successful publish. After that, the browser script keeps
    running during reconnection. Only the latest frame is retained, so missed frames are discarded.
    Pass an <code>AbortSignal</code> to stop startup waits or a running session. Exhausting the retry
    budget rejects <code>record()</code> and fails Playwright Test fixture teardown.
  </p>

  <h2 id="live-effects">Live effects</h2>
  <p>
    The stream follows <code>suitecut.selectPage()</code>, popup selection, and page closure. Idle
    pages repeat their latest frame. Capture pauses freeze the image while the broadcast clock
    continues. Zoom crops the encoded frames without changing website layout or mouse coordinates.
    Highlights, cursor movement, click pulses, typing, scrolling, and captions also appear live.
  </p>
  <p>
    <code>checkpoint()</code> holds the view without saving a clip. Final-render editing, result cards,
    and audio mixing are offline operations. The returned manifest is a session summary with no replay
    timeline. Closed-page history and completed events are discarded. Narration synthesis uses temporary
    files that are removed when synthesis completes.
  </p>

  <h2 id="verify-locally">Verify locally</h2>
  <CodeBlock
    code={`pnpm install --frozen-lockfile
pnpm exec playwright install chromium
pnpm test:stream:audio
pnpm test:stream:bitrate
pnpm test:stream:congestion`}
    label="Terminal"
    lang="bash"
  />
  <p>
    From the repository, this check starts a local RTMP receiver, exercises live effects and page
    switching, interrupts the receiver, and verifies sustained recovery. It also checks that no
    source artifacts remain. Receiver footage and screenshots are saved under
    <code>.suitecut/live-verification/</code>. Nothing is published externally.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
